        "<p><strong>The critical actions.</strong> Same-day bladder drainage and transfer in the newborn, because obstruction injures the kidneys by the hour; same-night treatment of cloudy effluent, because each day of peritonitis damages the membrane; cultures and antibiotics within the hour for catheter sepsis, because a child with a falling pressure is already septic; a pediatric order the adult template cannot reach, because the adult default causes disequilibrium and hypotension; the bladder before the transplant date and no paid donation, because a lost graft and an exploited donor are both irreversible; a confirmed first adult visit, because graft loss peaks at the age of transfer; and never letting coverage become a prescription.</p>",
